# The first member breaks and the member behind it does not depend on
# it: a branch verification over two changed portdirs with no edge
# between them, which is the road that produced the live observation
# this corpus was extended for — mise, unrelated to oniguruma6, came
# back "oniguruma6 fails to build; this member is untested" under the
# runner that stopped.
#
# The runner goes on now. mise's requires.1 is empty, so nothing blocks
# it; it is announced, linted and installed after jq's failure, and its
# own section is where its own lint line is read from. jq's failure is
# jq's and keeps the environment; mise's pass is mise's and would be
# published on. The aggregate is failed because one member failed, and
# that is the only thing the two members share.
# SYNTHESIZED from the cohort runner in internal/verify/tart/tart.go,
# not captured: see README.md.
members: jq mise
outcome: failed
jq.state: failed
jq.detail: Failed to build jq: command execution failed
jq.reported: failed
mise.state: passed
mise.lint: 1 warning
mise.reported: passed
